WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:16.689
RAE: The thought that I had, sitting here,

00:00:16.689 --> 00:00:17.970
while 

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:18.969
Nick made that

00:00:18.969 --> 00:00:20.170
was that

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:24.489
I think when you-- this course is
gonna be--

00:00:24.489 --> 00:00:27.630
not replicated, but it will go on in many,

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.560
many parts of the world in many schools.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.710
I think it would be a great idea if it began

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:36.590
with you-- in person if possible, or otherwise

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:39.450
through the magic of video--

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.469
giving this--

00:00:40.469 --> 00:00:43.220
the lecture you just gave,

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:45.120
which I think is a 

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.610
really good way of structuring

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:48.750
and purposing

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.710
a seminar like this. Now there may be
other seminars that

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:54.370
don't fit that template,

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.810
but I would urge you to do that. I mean,

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:58.690
goodness, I--

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.120
the idea that we can say how 

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.809
we're going to impact you in this course...

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:08.460
It's interesting, in fact-- I've taught, now,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.540
easily a hundred courses at Yale. 

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:17.120
And that's a question I've never been asked.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.700
And it's--

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.760
maybe-- 

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.580
well it's certainly-- the point certainly
is not

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:28.310
some sort of technical expertise.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:29.420
It is

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.650
some kind of cosmopolitan knowledge of

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:36.360
the role of faith in the very complex

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.470
history that you're going to be part of.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:40.619
And some of you will be,

00:01:40.619 --> 00:01:42.680
not just part of it, but influential

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.280
parts of it.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.979
And it seems quite likely that the

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:49.840
humanizing spirit-- maybe--

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:53.780
"humanizing," I guess, is tendentious in
this context,

00:01:53.780 --> 00:02:00.780
but I'll use it anyway-- the humanizing
spirit that is-- that pervades this seminar,

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:06.310
is a pretty good starting place for dealing
with difference. And--

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:10.399
I forget if it's point three or point four, but-- getting from

00:02:10.399 --> 00:02:12.409
grudging tolerance

00:02:12.409 --> 00:02:15.079
to mutual respect

00:02:15.079 --> 00:02:18.499
is no easy task

00:02:18.499 --> 00:02:20.379
in many of the world's

00:02:20.379 --> 00:02:22.189
arenas. 

00:02:22.189 --> 00:02:24.140
And it--I would say if you

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.749
carry that ambition and

00:02:26.749 --> 00:02:28.589
cultivate the skills--

00:02:28.589 --> 00:02:31.509
that by itself would be

00:02:31.509 --> 00:02:38.509
a worthwhile purpose for this course.

00:02:39.909 --> 00:02:44.489
VOLF: You know, I suppose I want to answer this

00:02:44.489 --> 00:02:46.920
in the way that--

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:51.730
so what makes me take this course? If I ask 
my question of myself-- why do I think this

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:52.890
is really

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.730
important? Why am I so excited about it?

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.149
What does it do to me?

00:02:57.149 --> 00:02:58.329
And maybe you can

00:02:58.329 --> 00:03:02.389
pick up something for this, for yourself, or
maybe not, right? That may be. But that--

00:03:02.389 --> 00:03:04.469
that's probably the way in which I want to

00:03:04.469 --> 00:03:06.200
answer it, and if you ask me,

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.729
why my passion about this course?

00:03:08.729 --> 00:03:11.749
I think I would say

00:03:11.749 --> 00:03:17.279
because I want to bring the idea

00:03:17.279 --> 00:03:19.479
of purpose, of the ends, 

00:03:19.479 --> 00:03:20.559
of human life,

00:03:20.559 --> 00:03:22.749
individual life,

00:03:22.749 --> 00:03:23.729
institutional

00:03:23.729 --> 00:03:25.569
life, organizational life,

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:29.539
to bear upon the functioning

00:03:29.539 --> 00:03:32.099
of our very complex world. 

00:03:32.099 --> 00:03:35.609
I'm really interested-- what really drives
me is

00:03:35.609 --> 00:03:37.790
the concept of human flourishing

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.909
in the context of a global common good.

00:03:40.909 --> 00:03:43.599
And in the world which is

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:45.199
interconnected, interdependent--

00:03:45.199 --> 00:03:47.060
different faiths with different visions

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:51.930
of human flourishing-- different visions of the
global common good--

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.680
living together side by side.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.019
And if we can learn how not to give up on asking the notion

00:03:58.019 --> 00:03:58.989
of purpose,

00:03:58.989 --> 00:04:01.370
asking the question of purpose,

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:05.539
and pursuing human flourishing that's broader
than just my own interest

00:04:05.539 --> 00:04:08.649
but at the same time learn how to live together

00:04:08.649 --> 00:04:11.749
in the way that is mutually enriching--

00:04:11.749 --> 00:04:13.079
what a world we would create!

00:04:13.079 --> 00:04:17.859
So if I ask myself why am I engaged with it, that's
why I'm engaged with it. I want to roll up my sleeves,

00:04:17.859 --> 00:04:19.319
make a better world,

00:04:19.319 --> 00:04:24.439
with people of different faiths living
together while not giving up.

00:04:24.439 --> 00:04:25.669
My

00:04:25.669 --> 00:04:26.639
notion

00:04:26.639 --> 00:04:29.520
of human flourishing derives from the venerable

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:30.590
faith tradition

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:33.790
and respecting others who have other venerable
traditions

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.579
as well. So I'm hoping

00:04:35.579 --> 00:04:37.260
that you'll go away

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.289
with the vision 

00:04:38.289 --> 00:04:39.960
of human flourishing,

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:45.639
with some kind of instruments to how to work
toward realizing that vision,

00:04:45.639 --> 00:04:48.520
and working together alongside others

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:54.569
toward that same goal.

00:04:54.569 --> 00:04:57.129
BLAIR: For me, I think it's very

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:59.150
simple. I'd like you to better

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.389
take out from this

00:05:00.389 --> 00:05:06.689
why this is such an important question. I think
it's as simple as that-- that it is really important.

00:05:06.689 --> 00:05:09.909
But secondly, and leading on from 

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:13.960
Doug and Miroslav--

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:20.599
I hope-- 'cause this is the very best thing about a university-- you can--

00:05:20.599 --> 00:05:23.120
probably when-- maybe Fred knows, because he's been out in the 

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.770
world and come back and so on, but--

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:29.119
the most important thing,

00:05:29.119 --> 00:05:30.349
I think,

00:05:30.349 --> 00:05:31.810
is to be able

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:34.789
always to gain fresh insights into the world.

00:05:34.789 --> 00:05:37.100
And if what this has done has made you think
about--

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.240
maybe your own faith,

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:42.099
and maybe your own faith and its place in the
world--

00:05:42.099 --> 00:05:46.190
and how it relates to other people-- then that's,
I think, something that's really worth

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:49.430
while. But I think that

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.449
the single most important thing you can

00:05:51.449 --> 00:05:54.299
get out of this is

00:05:54.299 --> 00:05:56.539
to understand that 

00:05:56.539 --> 00:05:58.020
without

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:03.509
a knowledge of this issue, and

00:06:03.509 --> 00:06:05.009
a belief, then, 

00:06:05.009 --> 00:06:10.129
that is the result of your knowledge, it's
important to act--

00:06:10.129 --> 00:06:11.129
if that's what 

00:06:11.129 --> 00:06:13.469
what you can get out of it, that's-- this is good. 

